---
import BaseLayout from '~/components/BaseLayout.astro';
import DocsShell from '~/components/DocsShell.astro';
import CodeBlock from '~/components/CodeBlock.astro';
import Callout from '~/components/Callout.astro';
import { SITE, VERSIONS } from '~/data/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Teptris JavaScript/TypeScript — TOML docs"
  description="The teptris npm package: libteptris compiled to WebAssembly — loads/dump/dumpJson with first-class TypeScript types, RFC 3339 datetimes, the full TOML 1.1 draft grammar, no fallback."
>
  <DocsShell
    crumb="Teptris — JavaScript/TypeScript"
    title={`Teptris — the npm package v${VERSIONS.tomlJs}`}
    lede={`libteptris v${VERSIONS.toml} compiled to WebAssembly (emscripten, ES module). One async init, three operations, first-class TypeScript declarations — and the same parse/emit behavior as the ruby, python and rust bindings.`}
  >
    <h2 id="install">Installation</h2>
    <CodeBlock lang="bash" code={`npm install teptris`} />
    <p>
      The package is ESM-only (<code>&quot;type&quot;: &quot;module&quot;</code>,
      Node ≥ 20, browsers, bundlers). It ships the wasm binary, the JS
      wrapper and the type declarations — a single self-contained
      package, no postinstall, no native modules.
    </p>

    <h2 id="usage">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="ts"
      code={`import { init } from "teptris";

const teptris = await init();

const doc = teptris.loads('title = "demo"\\npi = 3.5\\nat = 2026-10-09T12:00:00Z\\n');
// => { title: "demo", pi: 3.5, at: "2026-10-09T12:00:00Z" }

teptris.dump(doc);      // canonical TOML (RFC 3339 strings re-enter as datetimes)
teptris.dumpJson(doc);  // natural JSON — the string a host hands to JSON consumers
teptris.engineVersion();`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>loads</code> returns the natural-JSON view: real numbers,
      booleans, and RFC 3339 strings for datetimes; non-finite floats
      (nan/inf) become <code>null</code>. <code>dump</code> emits
      canonical TOML through the engine builder; <code>dumpJson</code>
      emits the same tree as natural JSON. Errors carry
      <code>line</code>/<code>column</code>.
    </p>
    <Callout kind="note">
      <p>
        The typed contract lives in the package: <code>init</code>,
        <code>initApi</code>, <code>TeptrisApi</code>,
        <code>TomlTable</code>, <code>TomlValue</code> and
        <code>TeptrisError</code>. The package&rsquo;s own test suite
        type-checks a strict <code>tsc</code> consumer on every run.
      </p>
    </Callout>

    <h2 id="descriptor">Descriptor plans</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="ts"
      code={`const plan = teptris.planBuild([
    "title",
    "tags",
    { name: "owner", rows: ["name", { name: "meta", kind: "raw" }] },
  ]);

const view = teptris.planWalk(plan, toml); // only planned keys
teptris.planFree(plan);`}
    />
    <p>
      Compile a plan once, walk any number of documents: only the
      planned keys cross the wasm boundary — unplanned keys are never
      materialized. Rows: a string name is a scalar;
      <code>kind: &quot;collection&quot;</code> walks an array;
      <code>kind: &quot;raw&quot;</code> takes the untouched subtree;
      <code>rows</code> walks a nested table. Typed as
      <code>PlanRowSpec</code> in the package.
    </p>

    <h2 id="performance">Performance</h2>
    <p>
      Against the JS ecosystem&rsquo;s parsers over the engine bench
      corpus: <strong>2–4× @iarna/toml</strong> — the long-standing
      standard, which also rejects mixed-type arrays that are legal
      TOML 1.0 — and <strong>parity with smol-toml</strong>, the modern
      fast pure-JS parser: teptris wins the datetime-heavy shapes
      (1.5×) and deep tables; smol wins string-heavy inputs, where the
      wasm→JS bridge prices every string. The tier&rsquo;s real edge
      is correctness: the <strong>full TOML 1.1 draft grammar</strong>
      with the same parse/emit behavior as the native bindings.
    </p>

    <h2 id="advanced">Advanced instantiation</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="ts"
      code={`import { initApi } from "teptris";
import createModule from "teptris/dist/teptris.mjs";

// for bundlers with their own wasm loading
const api = initApi(await createModule({ locateFile: ... }));`}
    />
    <p>
      <a href={`${SITE.githubTomlTs}`}>Source — teptris-ts</a>.
    </p>
  </DocsShell>
</BaseLayout>
